WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.036
(alarm clock buzzing)

00:00:01.036 --> 00:00:02.708
- [Ed] We usually get up about 7:00.

00:00:02.708 --> 00:00:04.798
- [Marsha] Yeah, and I
usually get up a little later.

00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:06.536
- [Ed] I make coffee for both of us.

00:00:06.536 --> 00:00:08.635
- [Marsha] I like honey
and cream in my coffee.

00:00:08.635 --> 00:00:11.598
- [Ed] And then, I almost
always drive to work.

00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:13.555
Our morning routine is quite mundane.

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:14.853
- [Marsha] Oh, yeah.

00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:17.531
One thing we're doing today
is the fire-breathing dragon,

00:00:17.531 --> 00:00:18.801
finishing off that.

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:20.890
- [Ed] Yeah, and I've
got some stuff to blood,

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.390
and some skulls, and pumpkins.

00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:27.651
- I'm Marsha, this is my
husband, Ed, and we run

00:00:27.651 --> 00:00:29.412
Distortions Unlimited.

00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:33.917
- We make monsters: zombies,
aliens, dragons, and beasts

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.476
of all kinds.

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:38.476
- Oh my. (laughing)

00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:41.818
Most of what we make is
scary, I will say that.

00:00:41.818 --> 00:00:45.698
We make monsters for
everyone from home haunter,

00:00:45.698 --> 00:00:49.355
all the way up to amusement
parks, and big events

00:00:49.355 --> 00:00:51.105
all around the world.

00:00:53.527 --> 00:00:56.234
We've been working together for 35 years.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.479
It's been glorious.

00:00:57.479 --> 00:00:59.221
- Yeah, wonderful.

00:00:59.221 --> 00:01:01.471
(laughing)

00:01:02.736 --> 00:01:04.985
- [Marsha] We started
out painting together.

00:01:04.985 --> 00:01:08.369
- [Ed] I fell in love very quickly.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:11.355
- [Marsha] We've been
married almost 25 years.

00:01:11.355 --> 00:01:13.570
- [Ed] We've found a way to work together.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.031
- [Marsha] I'm probably more
on the business side, and Ed is

00:01:17.031 --> 00:01:19.592
probably more into production.

00:01:19.592 --> 00:01:21.604
- [Ed] I can't tell you how
many people have told me

00:01:21.604 --> 00:01:25.161
I could never work with my
spouse, and that's too bad,

00:01:25.161 --> 00:01:29.328
because you miss half or more
of that whole person's life

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.762
if you don't.

00:01:31.762 --> 00:01:32.595
- Woo!

00:01:33.967 --> 00:01:37.262
(whimsical piano music)

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:39.727
- I think people expect us
to be a little bit weirder

00:01:39.727 --> 00:01:42.778
than we are; and we're actually
a little bit boring.

00:01:42.778 --> 00:01:47.319
When we get in the car
and go home, it's over.

00:01:47.319 --> 00:01:49.735
We love monsters, we just,
we've had enough of it

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.234
after a long day.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.390
There's a separation there.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.972
There has to be or you go crazy.

00:01:54.972 --> 00:01:56.527
If somebody walked into our
house, they wouldn't have

00:01:56.527 --> 00:01:57.906
a clue what we do.

00:01:57.906 --> 00:02:00.805
In fact, we keep it all kind of secret.

00:02:00.805 --> 00:02:03.212
Yeah, people are surprised
about that with us.

00:02:03.212 --> 00:02:04.879
We like it that way.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.770
It's really special to
do something you love

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.730
with somebody you love.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.348
- [Marsha] We make monsters,
but whatever our personalities

00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:19.390
kind of mesh with each
other, so it works out.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.958
- You know, you really can
establish a good relationship

00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:23.929
as you're dripping zombie blood.

00:02:23.929 --> 00:02:24.808
- Right.

00:02:24.808 --> 00:02:28.641
- That's the kind of
woman I need in my life.

